# Gaeil

> A named Python repo. This wrap keeps the Irish-facing name and points back to the source files.

## Purpose
Give a plain-language door to fitzyracing1/Gaeil so the project can be opened without guessing from the title alone.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the place for code.
2. Use this clone only to explain the idea in everyday words.
3. Send the reader back to the source for any run.

## Key ideas
- Gaeil (the project name)
- Wrap (this page explains; it does not replace)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/Gaeil
open_source()
read_python()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to the original repo”
2. read_python() → “the working files are Python there”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader needs the program → send them to the source
- If a reader needs the idea → stay on this listing

## What a person would notice
A named wrap that refuses to hide the original.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/Gaeil and read the README there.
